=== Phase 1 - boot status state contract (e32650b) ===
Added src/game/hud/bootStatus.ts as a pure loading -> ready | failed -> retrying
lifecycle with an injected retry callback, guarded late failure, and one-shot retry
semantics. 5 targeted tests. Coverage 94.44% statements / 88.88% branches / 85.71%
functions. No DOM behaviour in this phase.

=== Phase 2 - progressive town (39218bf) ===
Two-phase mount: mountTown mounts every ground quad, signals an onBaseReady seam,
then streams model placements in authored order; game.mount adds the group from that
seam so the base renders while models load. townRenderer.ts at 100% coverage across
all metrics, game.ts 94.01% / 86.16% / 90.36%. 16 town tests, 65 controller tests.

=== Phase 3 - non-blocking optional audio (eb0e252) ===
src/game/audio/sampleLoader.ts settles every clip with Promise.allSettled over
AudioEngine.load. A failed fetch or decode leaves one sound silent instead of
rejecting the boot fan-out as Promise.all did. Registry, URLs, decode path,
synthesized voices, mute, and unlock all unchanged; a later load can repopulate a
failed clip. sampleLoader.ts at 100% coverage.

=== Phase 4 - browser edge and failure recovery (3aef0cf) ===
src/game/hud/bootOverlay.ts is the DOM over bootStatus: a bouncing toy car while
loading, one large round-arrow retry on failure, no visible text. main.ts gains a
single try/catch around the driven and ready promises, gameplay input and the
vehicle HUD only after ready, and on failure stops the render loop, disconnects the
observer, disposes audio, and offers exactly one full-page reload. The one-shot
first-gesture audio unlock moved to a window-level pointerdown so a tap on the
overlay still unlocks.

=== Phase 5 - integration, docs, device ===
Production preview verified: first visit cleared the overlay with 6 HUD buttons,
service worker registered and active, 0 page errors; airplane-mode reopen with
navigator.onLine false still reached ready and kept animating; safe areas held at
810x1080 and 1080x810 with vehicles 91x91, ability 96x96, mute 72x72, parent gear
56x56, all fully in-viewport. Physical iPad 9th-generation: passed, owner-confirmed,
including after the review fixes.

=== Review pass 1 (7e00295) - 5 findings, all fixed ===
1. The one-shot first-gesture unlock was registered before the try and never removed
   on failure, so the retry tap called unlock(), which rebuilds the graph and made a
   fresh AudioContext on a disposed engine. PROVEN FIXED by instrumenting AudioContext
   construction: 1 before retry, 2 after reload, where the bug reads 3.
2. acknowledgeTouch() was implemented and unit-tested but never called from
   production, so a tap during loading produced no visual answer. This broke FR2 and
   AC3 explicitly. Now a 220ms Web Animations squash, restart-not-queue.
3. The empty catch {} logged nothing for a model that downloads and then fails to
   parse, so the troubleshooting doc's "check the console" advice was wrong for that
   whole class. Now logs "Tiny Town Explorers failed to start". A later
   TypeError: Failed to fetch was observed with a full stack through modelLibrary.
4. A leftover red-phase cast `mountTown as unknown as (...args: unknown[])` erased
   the signature of the API this track added, so it was not type-checked at its own
   test. The test now mocks the real four-argument signature.
5. Parent panel and install hint survived the failure path, frozen behind the retry
   icon by the stopped render loop. Now disposed and dismissed.

=== Review pass 2 (3b62885) - 3 findings, all fixed ===
6. The retry button listened only for pointerdown, leaving a focusable, aria-labelled
   control inert for Enter, Space, and assistive activation. Switched to click.
   PROVEN FIXED by counting navigations: Enter went 0 -> 1, pointer stayed at 1.
7. The squash overwrote the CSS bounce transform wholesale, snapping vertical offset
   to zero at t=0. Icon moved to an inner .boot__toy-face so the two compose.
8. The audio troubleshooting note described a console diagnostic that does not exist
   for decode failures, which Promise.allSettled swallows silently.

